et corner  screaming that sky  had become self-aware and that  terminators were coming for us all just  us okay  anyway box is hoping that you haven't  tired of stories of dystopian digital  futures with its new show next the  futuristic thriller stars John Slattery  as a tech entrepreneur who realizes that  an artificial intelligence application  he created could eventually lead to the  world's destruction in an era where we  already have smart homes our phones are  always listening to us and companies and  governments are doing who-knows-what  with the data it might be hard to get  viewers to worked up over the premise of  the show seriously have you kept up with  the news on this stuff this tech  dystopia looks too familiar we want to  see something with robots a son is being  asked to follow in his father's  footsteps the son rebels against being  pigeon-holed into a career that he  doesn't want reluctantly that son  eventually succumbs to his destiny  though it might be in a different way  than was originally envisioned many an  on-screen tale is told that story but  this fall when you tune into Fox's  prodigal son you'll be asked to consider  what if the family business was murder  good boy on the show Tom Paine plays the  son of a convicted serial killer asked  to track down other serial killers  imagine if Dexter's son eventually  became a homicide detective the show is  expected to have elements of dark comedy  which might work in its favor otherwise  this could end up is another in a long  line of homicidal maniac themed mystery  shows that get bogged down in the  premise that relies too heavily on a  weird father-son relationship and not  enough about catching the bad guys check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stop or coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

